    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d596">

                <pb facs="0570" n="558" xml:id="pg558"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">702.6261/37: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-07-08T14:00:00+03:00">July 8, 1940—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>831. A member of the German Embassy states that in accord with an agreement with
                    the Soviet Government the German Government has sent a Consul General to
                    Leningrad and is sending Consuls to Batum and Vladivostok.<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d596-f1"/> The informant added that for the time being the opening
                    of Consulates in Baku, Odessa and other places is not being considered. The
                    Soviet Government, it is understood, is opening consular offices in Vienna,
                    Hamburg and Koenigsberg.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d596-f1" n="19" xml:id="d596-f1-content">
                <p>A German Consulate General was established at Vladivostok previous to that
                    established by the American Government. For correspondence concerning
                    establishment of the American Consulate General, see <ref
                        target="frus1940v03#pg_460">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, pp.
                        460</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
